            "text": "```python\ndef reverse_list_elements(elements, punctuation):\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverse elements while keeping each punctuation mark\n    associated with its original element.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(elements) != len(punctuation):\n        raise ValueError(\"elements and punctuation must have the same length\")\n\n    pairs = list(zip(elements, punctuation))\n    reversed_pairs = pairs[::-1]\n\n    new_elements = [word for word, symbol in reversed_pairs]\n    new_punctuation = [symbol for word, symbol in reversed_pairs]\n\n    return new_elements, new_punctuation\n\n\n# Example\nelements = [\"Hello\", \"world\"]\npunctuation = [\"\", \"!\"]\n\nprint(reverse_list_elements(elements, punctuation))\n# ([\"world\", \"Hello\"], [\"!\", \"\"])\n```"
